<ns0:para xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167836518536">In the last example, we found <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>f</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> for a constant value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>. In the next example, we are asked to find <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> with values of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis> that are variables. We still follow the same procedure and substitute the variables in for the <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>.</ns0:para>

